4. **Why not higher?** While the paragraph includes citations (e.g., BitNet [11]), the citation-derived value is *not* the focus of the paragraph itself. The results (Figures 2 and 1) are the technical output, and the comparison is a necessary framing device—not the core innovation. This avoids overestimating citation_percentage (which would be >40% if the paragraph were primarily about literature review).

